\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### Hubble Time Conversion
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 ```\cb1 \
\cb3 H0 [km/s/Mpc] \uc0\u8594  H0 [s\u8315 \'b9]\cb1 \
\cb3 t_H = 1 / H0 [s]\cb1 \
\cb3 Convert to Gyr: 1 Gyr = 3.154 \'d7 10\'b9\uc0\u8310  s\cb1 \
\cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### Riemann Zeta Zeros
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 Using \cf6 \strokec6 `mpmath.zetazero(i)`\cf4 \strokec4  with 50 decimal place precision:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Returns complex number on critical line\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Extract imaginary part: \uc0\u947 _n = Im(\u950 (1/2 + i\u947 _n)) = 0\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Ordinates: \uc0\u947 \u8321  \u8776  14.134, \u947 \u8322  \u8776  21.022, ...\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### Relative Error Metric
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 ```\cb1 \
\cb3 rel_err = |\uc0\u964 \u8320  - \u964 _pred| / \u964 \u8320 \cb1 \
\cb3 ```\cb1 \
\
\cb3 Hit threshold (default): 1% (eps_hit = 0.01)\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### H0 Robustness
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 Test two scenarios:\cb1 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  H0 \'d7 (1 \uc0\u8722  0.02) = H0 \'d7 0.98\cb1 \
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  H0 \'d7 (1 + 0.02) = H0 \'d7 1.02\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf4 \cb3 For each, find best match in same family. If either \uc0\u8804  eps_hit, mark as "ok".\cb1 \
\
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0

\f0\b \cf2 \cb3 \strokec2 ### Determinism
\f1\b0 \cf4 \cb1 \strokec4 \
\pard\pardeftab720\partightenfactor0
\cf5 \cb3 \strokec5 -\cf4 \strokec4  Seed controls all random null trials\cb1 \
